2. The component treats appended samples as one continuous stream. The first sample after construction or clear() is sample 0, the next is sample 1, and so on. These sample numbers are used for column analysis and viewport positioning.






Compose Progressive Concurrent Spectrogram
Context
A Jetpack Compose component renders a live spectrogram timeline. Audio samples may be appended from any thread. The state object analyzes complete sample windows on background threads, commits finished spectrogram columns on the main thread, and the composable draws committed columns as a heatmap.
The hard part is concurrency correctness: analysis jobs may finish out of order, configuration may change while jobs are running, stale results must be rejected, zoomed-out rendering must preserve peaks, cache eviction must not corrupt visible output, and drawing/snapshotting must never deadlock.
