Requirements
Use Jetpack Compose Canvas, Android Bitmap/Canvas for snapshots, Kotlin standard library, and JDK concurrency primitives only. Do not use Android View, TextView, TextureView, SurfaceView, RenderThread, coroutines, RxJava, or third-party rendering libraries.
The state constructor must throw IllegalArgumentException if maxCachedColumns <= 0. Public methods may be called from any thread. Column commits and Compose-observed state mutations must happen on the main thread. Worker threads must not mutate Compose snapshot state directly.
Samples have absolute indices starting at 0 after construction or clear(). appendSamples appends all provided samples as one complete operation, copies the input array before returning, clamps values to [-1f, 1f], and treats NaN or infinite values as 0f.
setAnalysisConfig(windowSize, hopSize, bandCount) requires windowSize > 0, hopSize > 0, hopSize <= windowSize, bandCount > 0, and bandCount <= windowSize; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException. Changing the config invalidates all pending and committed columns.
Column k analyzes samples [k * hopSize, k * hopSize + windowSize). For rendering, column k represents [k * hopSize, (k + 1) * hopSize). A column may be scheduled only after its full analysis window exists.
Band energy is deterministic: split the analysis window into bandCount contiguous ranges; each band energy is the maximum absolute sample value in its range.
setViewport(firstSampleIndex, samplesPerPixel) requires finite samplesPerPixel > 0; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException. Pixel x represents [firstSampleIndex + x * samplesPerPixel, firstSampleIndex + (x + 1) * samplesPerPixel).
If a pixel intersects multiple committed columns, each band renders the maximum energy across those columns. Missing, pending, evicted, stale, or future ranges draw only the black background.
Energy is drawn as orange intensity: 0f is black and 1f is #FFFF9800. Band 0 is drawn at the bottom; bandCount - 1 is drawn at the top.
ProgressiveSpectrogram must not block waiting for analysis. It may schedule missing visible columns when its size or state revision changes, but repeated recompositions/draws must not schedule duplicate jobs for the same column and generation.
Analysis jobs must use immutable snapshots of sample data, config, and generation. A result may commit only if its generation, config, and column key are still current and pending.
clear() removes samples, pending columns, committed columns, and resets the next sample index to 0. Old worker completions must not repopulate the cache.
Committed columns are stored in an LRU cache capped by maxCachedColumns, except when all excess columns are visible in the current draw. Evict least-recently-used non-visible columns first. Columns visible in the current draw must not be evicted during that draw.
renderSnapshot(width, height) requires positive dimensions, renders into a new Bitmap from one immutable snapshot of committed columns and viewport values, does not call a composable, does not wait for workers or the main thread, and does not mutate state.
debugState() returns a stable snapshot without mutating state, scheduling jobs, waiting for workers, or exposing mutable internal collections. commitThreadIds records the thread id used for each committed column since construction or the latest clear(); every value must equal mainThreadId.
The implementation must not deadlock under concurrent appendSamples, setViewport, setAnalysisConfig, clear, composition/drawing, renderSnapshot, and worker completions. Output must be deterministic enough for Compose UI bitmap tests and Roborazzi screenshots.
Tests
Invalid inputs
Verify invalid maxCachedColumns, invalid analysis config including bandCount > windowSize, invalid samplesPerPixel, and invalid snapshot sizes throw IllegalArgumentException.
Sample copy, sanitization, partial windows, and duplicate scheduling
With windowSize = 4 and hopSize = 2, append 3 samples and verify no column is pending or committed. Append enough for 10 samples using values outside [-1, 1], NaN, and infinity; mutate the source array after append. Compose repeatedly at a viewport covering [0, 8). Verify only columns 0, 1, 2, and 3 are scheduled once, and rendered energies reflect copied sanitized values.
Out-of-order completion
Use a controlled executor. Schedule columns 0, 1, and 2, then complete jobs in order 2, 0, 1. Verify final rendering is ordered by column index, not completion order.
Clear rejects old workers
Start jobs, call clear(), complete old jobs, and verify no old columns commit. Append new samples after clear() and verify the timeline starts again at column 0.
Config change rejects stale columns
Start jobs with one config, call setAnalysisConfig with a different bandCount, complete old jobs, and verify old results do not commit.
Zoomed-out peak preservation and band orientation
Place one high-energy column inside a pixel bucket with low-energy neighbors. Use a high samplesPerPixel so the bucket intersects multiple columns. Verify max aggregation keeps the spike visible. Verify band 0 appears at the bottom and the highest band appears at the top.
Missing and future ranges draw background
Use a viewport spanning before sample 0 and beyond the newest samples. Verify missing regions remain black.
Main-thread commit
Complete jobs from worker threads, run pending main-thread tasks, call debugState(), and verify every commitThreadIds entry equals mainThreadId.
LRU eviction
Use a small cache. Render several columns, pan so some become non-visible, render more columns, and verify least-recently-used non-visible columns are evicted before visible columns.
Visible protection
Set maxCachedColumns smaller than the visible column count. Verify visible columns survive the current draw even if the cache temporarily exceeds the limit.
Snapshot safety
Call renderSnapshot from the main thread under a timeout while jobs are pending. Verify it returns without waiting and does not mutate debugState().
Snapshot consistency during viewport race
Run renderSnapshot while another thread changes viewport. Verify the result corresponds to either the old viewport or the new viewport, never mixed viewport values.
Stress race
Randomly interleave appendSamples, viewport changes, config changes, clear, composition/drawing, renderSnapshot, and out-of-order job completions. Verify no crashes, no deadlocks, no stale commits, and cache rules hold.
Roborazzi visual regression
Capture before jobs complete, after partial commit, after all visible columns commit, and a zoomed-out spike case. Verify progressive fill, no stale artifacts, stable orange intensity, and spike preservation.




